    "Chlorine has two stable isotopes, <sup>35</sup>Cl (75.8%) and <sup>37</sup>Cl (24.2%). Bromine also has two, <sup>79</sup>Br (50.7%) and <sup>81</sup>Br (49.3%). For a diatomic molecule X<sub>2</sub>, the chance of each combination is found by multiplying the abundances, just like a Punnett square. Figure 1 shows the measured spectrum of Br<sub>2</sub>.",
