    "Thiosulfate is used because it reacts quickly and completely with iodine, and its solutions can be standardized against a known oxidizing agent. The titration measures the total oxidizing capacity of the sample, often reported as available chlorine.",
    "The molar mass of NaOCl is 74.4 g mol⁻¹. Infection-control guidelines call for a bleach solution of at least 1000 ppm (0.1% by mass) of available chlorine for routine disinfection.",
